<title>GREECE: Greek 1M ATHIBOR firms to 13.45 from 13.37pct.</title>
<headline>Greek 1M ATHIBOR firms to 13.45 from 13.37pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens Interbank Offered Rate (Athibor) for one month rose to 13.45 percent from 13.37 percent on Monday and the bid rate (Athibid) firmed to 12.96 from 12.87 percent.</p>
<p>ATHIBOR</p>
<p> DATE     1-MTH   2-MTH   3-MTH   6-MTH   9-MTH   12-MTH</p>
<p> Nov  18  13.45   13.40   13.33   13.29   13.36   13.36</p>
<p> Nov  15  13.37   13.31   13.25   13.24   13.30   13.32</p>
<p> Nov  14  13.72   13.69   13.63   13.53   13.53   13.54</p>
<p> Nov  13  13.94   13.91   13.84   13.74   13.71   13.69</p>
<p> Nov  12  14.01   13.99   13.91   13.81   13.79   13.76</p>
<p> Nov  11  13.38   13.38   13.38   13.40   13.40   13.42</p>
<p> Nov  08  13.32   13.32   13.32   13.35   13.35   13.38</p>
<p> Nov  07  13.32   13.32   13.32   13.34   13.35   13.38</p>
<p>ATHIBID</p>
<p> Nov  18  12.96   12.92   12.84   12.81   12.84   12.84</p>
<p> Nov  15  12.87   12.81   12.76   12.74   12.78   12.79</p>
<p> Nov  14  13.19   13.16   13.11   13.02   12.99   13.01</p>
<p> Nov  13  13.35   13.32   13.27   13.17   13.14   13.11</p>
<p> Nov  12  13.35   13.33   13.27   13.17   13.14   13.12</p>
<p> Nov  11  12.89   12.89   12.89   12.90   12.89   12.90</p>
<p> Nov  08  12.82   12.82   12.82   12.84   12.85   12.87</p>
<p> Nov  07  12.82   12.82   12.82   12.83   12.85   12.86</p>
<p>Note: ATHIBOR is Greece's official reference rate. It comprises 13 leading state and private banks committed to quoting their rates by 0900 GMT every day.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
